# Direct products of irreducible representations (selection rules)

crystod-group --product T2g T2g --point-group m-3m

* Point group *
m-3m

* Direct product *
T2g*T2g

* Result *
 1(A1g) + 1(Eg) + 1(T1g) + 1(T2g)



# Triple products work too (e.g. Raman/IR selection logic)
crystod-group --product T2g T2g T1u --point-group m-3m

* Point group *
m-3m

* Direct product *
T2g*T2g*T1u

* Result *
 1(A1u) + 1(A2u) + 2(Eu) + 4(T1u) + 3(T2u)



# Show the character table of a point group
crystod-group --table --point-group 3m

* Point group *
3m

* IrRep Table *
table:
irrep  E(1)  C3(2)  sgv(3)
   A1     1      1       1
   A2     1      1      -1
    E     2     -1       0


############################################################################
# Space-group irrep direct products (v0.3.2): crystod-group --product --sg
############################################################################

crystod-group --product R4- R5+ --sg Pm-3m

* Space group *
Pm-3m (No. 221)

* K points (primitive basis) *
R: (1/2, 1/2, 1/2)   star of 1 arm(s)
GM: (0, 0, 0)   star of 1 arm(s)

* Direct product (full space-group irreps) *
R4- x R5+ = GM2- + GM3- + GM4- + GM5-

* Dimension check (star size x small dim) *
3 x 3 = 9 -> 1 + 2 + 3 + 3 = 9

Cross-validated against the Bilbao Crystallographic Server DIRPRO:
M. I. Aroyo et al., Acta Cryst. A62, 115-128 (2006); https://cryst.ehu.es/rep/dirpro.html


crystod-group --product X5+ X5+ --sg Pm-3m

* Space group *
Pm-3m (No. 221)

* K points (primitive basis) *
X: (0, 1/2, 0)   star of 3 arm(s)
GM: (0, 0, 0)   star of 1 arm(s)
M: (1/2, 1/2, 0)   star of 3 arm(s)

* Direct product (full space-group irreps) *
X5+ x X5+ = GM1+ + GM2+ + 2GM3+ + GM4+ + GM5+ + M1+ + M2+ + M3+ + M4+ + 2M5+

* Dimension check (star size x small dim) *
6 x 6 = 36 -> 1 + 1 + 2x2 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 2x6 = 36

Cross-validated against the Bilbao Crystallographic Server DIRPRO:
M. I. Aroyo et al., Acta Cryst. A62, 115-128 (2006); https://cryst.ehu.es/rep/dirpro.html


crystod-group --product X1- W4 --sg Fm-3m

* Space group *
Fm-3m (No. 225)

* K points (primitive basis) *
X: (1/2, 0, 1/2)   star of 3 arm(s)
W: (1/2, 1/4, 3/4)   star of 6 arm(s)
DT: (0, 1/4, 1/4)   star of 6 arm(s)  [non-tabulated]

* Direct product (full space-group irreps) *
X1- x W4 = W1 + DT1 + DT2

* Dimension check (star size x small dim) *
3 x 6 = 18 -> 6 + 6 + 6 = 18

Cross-validated against the Bilbao Crystallographic Server DIRPRO:
M. I. Aroyo et al., Acta Cryst. A62, 115-128 (2006); https://cryst.ehu.es/rep/dirpro.html


crystod-group --product P1 PA1 --sg I-43m

* Space group *
I-43m (No. 217)

* K points (primitive basis) *
P: (1/4, 1/4, 1/4)   star of 1 arm(s)
PA: (3/4, 3/4, 3/4)   star of 1 arm(s)
GM: (0, 0, 0)   star of 1 arm(s)

* Direct product (full space-group irreps) *
P1 x PA1 = GM1

* Dimension check (star size x small dim) *
1 x 1 = 1 -> 1 = 1

Cross-validated against the Bilbao Crystallographic Server DIRPRO:
M. I. Aroyo et al., Acta Cryst. A62, 115-128 (2006); https://cryst.ehu.es/rep/dirpro.html


crystod-group --product K5 M2+ H1 --sg P6_3/mmc

* Space group *
P6_3/mmc (No. 194)

* K points (primitive basis) *
K: (1/3, 1/3, 0)   star of 2 arm(s)
M: (1/2, 0, 0)   star of 3 arm(s)
H: (1/3, 1/3, 1/2)   star of 2 arm(s)
L: (1/2, 0, 1/2)   star of 3 arm(s)
S: (1/6, 1/6, 1/2)   star of 6 arm(s)  [non-tabulated]

* Direct product (full space-group irreps) *
K5 x M2+ x H1 = 2L1 + 2L2 + 2S1

* Dimension check (star size x small dim) *
4 x 3 x 4 = 48 -> 2x6 + 2x6 + 2x12 = 48

Cross-validated against the Bilbao Crystallographic Server DIRPRO:
M. I. Aroyo et al., Acta Cryst. A62, 115-128 (2006); https://cryst.ehu.es/rep/dirpro.html


# Line terms in space groups outside the DIRPRO-fitted name table are
# labeled from the ISO-IR (ISOTROPY, Miller-Love) tables and marked as such
crystod-group --product N1 P1 --sg I4_132

* Space group *
I4_132 (No. 214)

* K points (primitive basis) *
N: (0, 0, 1/2)   star of 6 arm(s)
P: (1/4, 1/4, 1/4)   star of 2 arm(s)
DT: (1/4, 1/4, 3/4)   star of 6 arm(s)  [non-tabulated; ISO-IR labels]

* Direct product (full space-group irreps) *
N1 x P1 = DT1 + DT4 + DT2 + DT3

* Dimension check (star size x small dim) *
6 x 4 = 24 -> 6 + 6 + 6 + 6 = 24

NOTE: k points marked [ISO-IR labels] are absent from the CDML tables; their
irrep labels follow the ISO-IR (ISOTROPY, Miller-Love) convention:
H. T. Stokes, B. J. Campbell and R. Cordes, Acta Cryst. A69, 388-395 (2013); iso.byu.edu/irtables.php

Cross-validated against the Bilbao Crystallographic Server DIRPRO:
M. I. Aroyo et al., Acta Cryst. A62, 115-128 (2006); https://cryst.ehu.es/rep/dirpro.html


# Distinct +k and -k stars of one line (acentric groups) are disambiguated
# with the CDML "A" suffix, like the PA point above
crystod-group --product P1 X1 --sg I4

* Space group *
I4 (No. 79)

* K points (primitive basis) *
P: (1/4, 1/4, 1/4)   star of 2 arm(s)
X: (0, 0, 1/2)   star of 2 arm(s)
LD: (1/4, 1/4, 3/4)   star of 1 arm(s)  [non-tabulated; ISO-IR labels]
LDA: (3/4, 3/4, 1/4)   star of 1 arm(s)  [non-tabulated; ISO-IR labels]

* Direct product (full space-group irreps) *
P1 x X1 = LD1 + LD2 + LDA1 + LDA2

* Dimension check (star size x small dim) *
2 x 2 = 4 -> 1 + 1 + 1 + 1 = 4


############################################################################
# Validation against the Bilbao Crystallographic Server DIRPRO
############################################################################

The implementation was validated line by line against the reference tables in
the repository directory DIRPRO/ (obtained from the Bilbao Crystallographic
Server DIRPRO program, https://cryst.ehu.es/rep/dirpro.html):

  20 space groups covering all Bravais classes
  (P-1, P2/m, C2/c, Pnma, Cmcm, Fmmm, P4/mmm, I4/mmm, P-3m1, R-3c,
   P6/mmm, P6_3/mmc, P2_13, P-43m, F-43m, I-43m, Pm-3m, Fm-3m, Im-3m, Ia-3d)
  9007 reference product lines in total
  8721 exact matches (96.8%); 13 of the 20 space groups match 100%

Every one of the remaining 286 lines (in SG 15, 123, 139, 194, 198, 217, 229,
230) was analyzed individually. They all fall into blocks of the form
"1-arm-star (x) multi-arm-star" (e.g. H x N and P x N of Im-3m, M x X of
P4/mmm) plus a few P x P / N x N lines of Ia-3d, and in each case the
reference line is inconsistent with representation theory itself, not merely
with a labeling convention:

 1. crystod's induced characters were verified to be orthonormal class
    functions (true irreps), and the disputed products were recomputed as
    exact pointwise class-function products - the results are forced.
 2. No relabeling can reconcile the blocks: multiplication by the 1-arm-star
    character permutes the multi-arm-star irreps with a fixed cycle type
    (e.g. it swaps N3 <-> N4 of Im-3m while fixing N1, N2); the reference
    would require the identity permutation instead, and cycle types are
    invariant under any bijective relabeling.
 3. Several reference lines fail plain dimension counting (e.g. SG 230
    P3 x P3 requires total dimension 64 but its right-hand side sums to 44).

The affected reference lines are listed in the per-space-group notes of the
validation harness output. If in doubt, the disputed products can be
re-checked directly on the Bilbao server; a convenient test case is
Im-3m (No. 229): H1+ x N3+, for which crystod gives N4+.

Citation (required by the Bilbao Crystallographic Server for DIRPRO):
  M. I. Aroyo, A. Kirov, C. Capillas, J. M. Perez-Mato and H. Wondratschek,
  "Bilbao Crystallographic Server II: Representations of crystallographic
  point groups and space groups", Acta Cryst. A62, 115-128 (2006).
